# Build output.
#
# The binary pattern is anchored. A bare `relab` matches at any depth, which
# silently excluded cmd/relab/ — the program's entry point — from the
# repository. Nothing local caught it, because the file was on disk; CI failed
# on a checkout that had never contained it.
/bin/
/dist/
/relab

# Test and benchmark output
*.out
/coverage.*
/bench-results/

# Local environment
.env
.env.local

# Dashboard
/web/node_modules/
/web/.next/
/web/out/
/web/next-env.d.ts
/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# Credentials. This repository is public; nothing below may ever be committed.
#
# Codex signs in with ChatGPT and caches the login in the user's private
# ~/.codex directory. .codex/ here holds only project configuration and agent
# definitions, so the credential files are excluded by name in case a Codex
# run ever writes them into the project directory.
.codex/auth.json
**/auth.json
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!web/**/*.key.ts
id_rsa*
*credentials*.json
